# tests/recursion/k69.rxt -- K69 (docs/dev/known_issues.md), [PATFACTS] step
# 3.5: a call's NULLABILITY is the LEAST call-graph fixpoint.
#
# HAND-WRITTEN, NOT GENERATED, and every expectation below was read off
# libpcre2 10.46 BEFORE it was written: a light probe on the reference box
# through the committed ctypes binding
# (docs/design/subroutines_measurements/probes/sr_oracle.py, `search` from
# offset 0), transcript in docs/dev/lanes/k69fix_report.md §3. pcrec was not
# asked. Like the rest of this directory there is no python arm (python's
# `re` has no subroutine call). It is not in gen_corpus.py because that
# generator's cells are its own lane's record and re-running it re-measures
# all of them; this file is one fix's regression.
#
# WHAT MOVED. `u.call.nonnullable` used to be the emitter's own fixpoint,
# iterated from "nullable" UP -- the GREATEST fixpoint -- so a callee in a
# cycle whose only escape runs through the call read nullable, and a
# quantifier over it got an empty-iteration guard it can never need
# (`(a|(?1))`'s group is `{a}`). It is now `minw != 0`, published by
# src/opt/callgraph.c before the E1 seal: exact. The guard costs a slot and a
# test, never an answer, so this file's job is the converse: the guard's
# REMOVAL must not change an answer, and the guard must STAY where the callee
# really is nullable. The compile-time half -- the nullability itself, read
# through the one function the guard and the E1 fact both ask -- is
# tests/codegen/run_facts_checks.sh [facts-e1]'s call rows.
#
# THE WITNESSES ARE LAZY OR COUNTED ON PURPOSE. Under a greedy quantifier the
# loop always tries one more iteration at the end of the run, `a` fails there
# and the left recursion `(?1)` re-enters at the same position: libpcre2
# answers rc -52 ("nested recursion at the same subject position"), so no
# oracle expectation exists (`^(a|(?1))*$` on "" / "a" / "aa", measured). pcrec
# answers those cells identically before and after K69 (a match on "aa":
# the d27 corpus's finding-4 class, tests/recursion/CLAUDE.md). A lazy
# quantifier reaches its follow first, so the cells below are real matches.

# ====================================================================
# THE WITNESSES: a quantifier over a left-recursive callee whose language
# does not contain the empty string. Each lost its guard at K69.
# ====================================================================

pattern (a|(?1))*?b
features recursion
engine vm
m "aab" 0 3
g 1 1 2
m "b" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1

pattern (a|(?1))+?b
features recursion
engine vm
m "ab" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "aaab" 0 4
g 1 2 3

pattern (a|(?1)){2,}?c
features recursion
engine vm
m "aac" 0 3
g 1 1 2
m "aaac" 0 4
g 1 2 3

# two calls in the recursive branch: still no base case through them.
pattern (a|(?1)(?1))*?b
features recursion
engine vm
m "aaab" 0 4
g 1 2 3
m "b" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1

# the same shape reached through a DEFINE, direct and indirect (g -> h -> g).
pattern (?(DEFINE)(?<g>a|(?&g)))x(?&g)*?y
features recursion,named-groups
engine vm
m "xaay" 0 4
g 1 -1 -1
m "xy" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1

pattern (?(DEFINE)(?<g>a|(?&h))(?<h>(?&g)))x(?&g)*?y
features recursion,named-groups
engine vm
m "xaay" 0 4
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 -1 -1
m "xy" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 -1 -1

# ground truth for "the language is {a}": the group matches `a`, never empty.
pattern ^(a|(?1))$
features recursion
engine vm
m "a" 0 1
g 1 0 1

# ====================================================================
# THE CONTROLS. The guard must STAY on a callee that is really nullable,
# including one whose nullability runs through a cycle.
# ====================================================================

pattern (?(DEFINE)(?<g>a?))(?&g)*
features recursion,named-groups
engine vm
m "aaa" 0 3
g 1 -1 -1
m "" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1

# g is nullable only through h (h = b?): the least fixpoint still finds it.
pattern (?(DEFINE)(?<g>(?&h)|a)(?<h>b?))(?&g)*
features recursion,named-groups
engine vm
m "bba" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 -1 -1
m "a" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 -1 -1

pattern ^(a?)(?1)*$
features recursion
engine vm
m "aaa" 0 3
g 1 0 1
m "" 0 0
g 1 0 0

# lane pf35's controls: a call that is not the cycle's only escape, never
# guarded before or after.
pattern (a(?1)?)*
features recursion
engine vm
m "aaa" 0 3
g 1 0 3
m "" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1

pattern (a|b(?1))*
features recursion
engine vm
m "abba" 0 4
g 1 1 4
m "c" 0 0
g 1 -1 -1

# ====================================================================
# THE E1 WITNESSES (pf35's M2): a pattern whose non-nullability comes through
# a call. At K69's swap build the E1 fact read these as nullable; the fix
# publishes the call's answer before the seal, so it reads "no" and the
# answers are the ordinary ones. The DEFINE cell also runs under utf8, where a
# wrong "yes" would have added the [K50] start gate.
# ====================================================================

pattern (a)?(?1)
features recursion
engine vm
m "aa" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "a" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
n "b"

pattern (?:(a)|)(?1)
features recursion
engine vm
m "aa" 0 2
g 1 0 1
m "a" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
n "b"

pattern (?(DEFINE)(?<g>a))(?&g)
features recursion,named-groups
m "a" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
m "ba" 1 2
g 1 -1 -1
n "b"

pattern (?(DEFINE)(?<g>a))(?&g)
features recursion,named-groups
encoding utf8
m "a" 0 1
g 1 -1 -1
m "ba" 1 2
g 1 -1 -1
n "b"
